"""Validate source coverage/CCD evidence and show the conservative repair."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
from cover import OUT,scan
r=json.loads((OUT/'verification.json').read_text());proof=json.loads((OUT/'geometry-verification.json').read_text());ccd=json.loads((OUT/'native-ccd-result.json').read_text());renders=json.loads((OUT/'renders.json').read_text());assert len(renders['views'])==36
for row in renders['views']:assert scan.digest(Path(row['path']))==row['sha256']
for path,h in r['input_pins'].items():assert scan.digest(Path(path))==h
assert scan.digest(Path(r['candidate_collision']))==r['candidate_sha256']
assert ccd['exit_code']==0 and ccd['temporary_test_removed']and scan.digest(OUT/'native-ccd-fixture.txt')==ccd['fixture_sha256']
assert '376 shots passed' in (OUT/'native-ccd.log').read_text()
paths={bank:{scope:{view:{stage:str(OUT/f'{bank}-{scope}-{view}-{stage}.webp')for stage in ['source','previous','candidate']}for view in ['oblique','face','reverse']}for scope in ['hub','bank']}for bank in ['bank-a','bank-b']}
html='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><style>
body{font-family:var(--font-sans);font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--foreground)}p{margin:0 0 12px}.controls{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:14px 0}select{font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--background);padding:7px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);max-width:100%}.images{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px}figure{margin:0}figcaption{margin-bottom:6px}img{width:100%;display:block;border-radius:var(--radius)}.muted{color:var(--muted-foreground);font-size:13px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:13px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:8px 4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}.note{padding:16px;background:var(--card);border-radius:var(--radius);margin:14px 0}</style></head><body>
<p><strong>Fixed the missing projectile coverage.</strong><br>The spoke hulls now enclose their complete original triangles, with outward padding. The center stays filled and the visuals stay unchanged.</p>
<div class="controls"><select id="reference" aria-label="Reference"><option value="previous">Previous trimmed fit</option><option value="source">Detailed collision</option></select><select id="bank" aria-label="Bank"><option value="bank-a">Bank A</option><option value="bank-b">Bank B</option></select><select id="scope" aria-label="Scope"><option value="hub">Fixed hub</option><option value="bank">With rotating arms</option></select><select id="camera" aria-label="Camera"><option value="oblique">Oblique</option><option value="face">Face</option><option value="reverse">Reverse</option></select></div>
<div class="images"><figure><figcaption id="beforeLabel">Previous trimmed fit</figcaption><img id="before" alt="Prior collision reference"></figure><figure><figcaption>Enclosing solids</figcaption><img id="after" alt="Full-depth enclosing spoke hulls"></figure></div><p class="muted" style="margin-top:8px">Blue: reference collision. Orange: enclosing hulls. Grey long arms stay exact. All visual bytes remain unchanged.</p>
<table><tr><th>Check</th><th>Result</th></tr><tr><td>Complete source triangles enclosed</td><td>18,135 / 18,135</td></tr><tr><td>Minimum margin after GLB reopen</td><td>0.249921 mm</td></tr><tr><td>Directional ray checks</td><td>187,662; zero misses</td></tr><tr><td>Native projectile CCD tests</td><td>376 / 376 passed</td></tr></table>
<div class="note"><strong>Coverage is checked over whole triangles.</strong> Every original triangle has all three vertices inside one convex solid, so the entire face is covered. Each spoke also overlaps the filled center. This prevents new geometric pass-through gaps in the solid hub and spoke surfaces.</div>
<p>The native physics test fired both projectile sizes (16.8 and 42.5 mm) at 12–40 m/s through 94 forward, reverse and oblique trajectories, at 128 Hz. Every shot produced collision response before passing the obstruction.</p>
<p>Still 13 hulls and no fixed-hub mesh triangles. The full spoke depth is restored; the earlier 5 mm rotor-clearance claim no longer applies. Full-field kinematic/scoring integration remains to be checked.</p>
<p class="muted">The test loads native hulls directly into WorldPhysics; grouped field loading is still outstanding. No assets are installed. Remaining mesh counts stay unchanged; the Rune diagnostic preview adds 1,128 triangles. The temporary simulator test was removed, leaving its worktree clean.</p>
<script>const paths=PATHS;function update(){const p=paths[bank.value][scope.value][camera.value];before.src=p[reference.value];after.src=p.candidate;beforeLabel.textContent=reference.selectedOptions[0].text;}for(const id of ['reference','bank','scope','camera'])document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('change',update);update();console.log('Conservative hub coverage + native CCD verification');</script></body></html>'''.replace('PATHS',json.dumps(paths))
(OUT/'gallery.html').write_text(html)
hashes={str(p.relative_to(OUT)):scan.digest(p)for p in OUT.rglob('*')if p.is_file()and p.name not in ['gallery.html','final-verification.json']}
(OUT/'final-verification.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(geometry=proof,native_ccd=ccd,matched_images=36,artifact_sha256=hashes,installed=False),indent=2)+'\n');print('Verified full coverage, 376 native shots and 36 matched images.')
